prompts.template:
Draft a reply to this customer message for {brand_name}.

Customer message:
{customer_message}

Facts I have confirmed:
{order_facts}

What policy allows me to offer:
{policy_options}

Brand voice: {brand_voice}

Rules:
- Acknowledge the problem in one sentence. One apology only.
- Give the facts and the next step with a date or timeframe.
- Offer only what's listed in policy. Don't promise delivery dates the courier hasn't given.
- Under 130 words. Sign off as {agent_first_name}.

I'm working in {app}. Write a formula for this:

What the data looks like now: {current_data}
What I need: {desired_result}
Where the formula goes: {target_cell}

Rules:
- Use functions that work in {app}.
- Explain each part of the formula in one line.
- Tell me which inputs would break it.

Write a Google Apps Script for this spreadsheet.

Tabs and columns: {sheet_structure}
What I do by hand now: {manual_steps}
When it should run: {schedule}

Requirements:
- One main function I can run from the Apps Script editor.
- Read and write in bulk with getValues and setValues, not cell by cell.
- Log how many rows it changed.
- Add a DRY_RUN setting at the top that logs what would change without writing.
- Explain how to set up the time-driven trigger.

prompts.example_output:
const DRY_RUN = true;

function archiveOldRows() {
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActive();
  const raw = ss.getSheetByName('Raw');
  const archive = ss.getSheetByName('Archive');
  const [header, ...rows] = raw.getDataRange().getValues();
  const today = new Date();
  today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

  const move = rows.filter(r => r[0] instanceof Date && r[0] < today);
  const keep = rows.filter(r => !(r[0] instanceof Date && r[0] < today));
  console.log(`${move.length} rows to archive, ${keep.length} stay`);
  if (DRY_RUN || !move.length) return;

  archive.getRange(archive.getLastRow() + 1, 1, move.length, header.length).setValues(move);
  raw.getRange(2, 1, rows.length, header.length).clearContent();
  if (keep.length) raw.getRange(2, 1, keep.length, header.length).setValues(keep);
}

Trigger: in the editor go to Triggers > Add trigger > archiveOldRows > Time-driven > Day timer > 6am to 7am. Check the project time zone is Australia/Melbourne under Project Settings.

prompts.template:
Write a {channel} message announcing a process change to {audience}.

What's changing: {change}
Starts: {start_date}
Why: {reason}
What people need to do: {actions}
Where to ask questions: {contact}

Format:
- First line says what changes and when.
- Then "What you need to do" as 2-4 bullets.
- Then one line on why.
- Under 120 words. No "exciting news" or "we're thrilled".

Turn these rough meeting notes into a follow-up message.

Meeting: {meeting_name}, {date}
Attendees: {attendees}
Notes:
{notes}

Format:
Decisions: bullets
Actions: table with Action | Owner | Due date
Open questions: bullets, or "None"

Rules: only include owners and dates that are in the notes. If an action has no owner or date, write "TBC" so I can fill it in.

Turn these notes into a standard operating procedure draft.

Process: {process_name}
Who does it: {roles}
Tools used: {tools}
Rough notes or transcript:
{notes}

Use this structure:
Purpose, Scope, Roles, Tools, Definitions, Procedure (numbered steps, each starting with a verb), Decision points (as "If... then..."), SLAs, Escalation, Common mistakes.

Rules:
- One action per step.
- Mark anything missing from my notes as [TO CONFIRM] instead of guessing.
